summary:
- topic: Graduation Planning for 2026 and 2027
  text: SPHS Principal Sarah Glenn presented graduation plans, highlighting a rain-date
    strategy for Graduation 2026 at Martin Field and a proposed move to the Cross
    Insurance Arena for Graduation 2027 due to athletic complex construction.
- topic: South Portland Middle School Field Remediation
  text: Director Mike Nalli updated the board on the SPMS Field, outlining a spring
    remediation plan involving aeration, overseeding, and fertilization, while addressing
    concerns over soil compaction, rocks, and funding responsibility.
- topic: Immigration Enforcement and Student Safety
  text: The board and public discussed the district's 'Strengthening Our Community
    Through Belonging' initiative, with citizens and staff calling for accelerated
    training and clearer protocols to protect vulnerable families from ICE activity.
- topic: FY2026 Budget Projections and Public Forum
  text: Finance Chair Ms. Holman reported on the district's budget status, projecting
    a potential deficit, while Superintendent Dr. Entwistle promoted the upcoming
    Public School Budget Forum on January 22nd to gather community input.
- topic: Superintendent Search Progress
  text: The board approved contracts and expenses with Zeal for the Superintendent
    Search, including national advertising with AASA and comprehensive background
    checks for finalists, despite some discussion regarding additional fees.
- topic: School Calendar Postponement
  text: The board voted to postpone the first reading of the School Calendar for the
    2026-27 School Year to negotiate the impact of an additional school day with the
    service employees' union.
