  seconds: 1524
  topic: South Portland Middle School Field Update (Mike Nalli)
  desc: Director Mike Nalli provided an update on the SPMS Field spring remediation
    plan, which includes aeration, overseeding, and fertilization. He reported that
    soil core samples met specifications but showed heavy compaction, and noted that
    the district is withholding funds from the contractor until the field is playable.
  children: []
- time: 0:29:44
  seconds: 1784
  topic: Board Discussion on SPMS Field Remediation
  desc: The board debated the quality of the SPMS Field, discussing soil compaction,
    weed management, and potential legal action against the contractor.
  children:
  - seconds: 1784
    speaker: Tyler Smith
    text: Smith shared his professional expertise as an arborist, discussing soil
      compaction and the potential need for an herbicide waiver to manage weed growth.
      He expressed concern that spring fertilization without weed control might support
      weed growth instead of grass.
  - seconds: 1953
    speaker: Eleni Richardson
    text: Richardson asked if redoing the field entirely was considered and questioned
      whether the contractor met the original specifications. She noted that the field
      was reportedly filled with rocks and compaction.
  - seconds: 2178
    speaker: Ms. Holman
    text: Holman criticized the field's substandard quality, called for more transparency,
      and suggested the district should consider legal action. She argued that the
      district deserved better than a fluffed-up field.
  - seconds: 2344
    speaker: Dr. Entwistle
    text: Dr. Entwistle agreed with the need for taxpayer representation and offered
      to look into adding someone to the oversight group. He welcomed the energy and
      focus on resolving the field issues.
  - seconds: 2372
    speaker: Rosemarie DeAngelis
    text: DeAngelis advised that board members should not be directly involved in
      the operational oversight meetings. She stated that operational issues fall
      under the superintendent's purview.
  - seconds: 2468
    speaker: George Risch
    text: Risch attempted to ask Tyler Smith if adding more soil would be a good solution,
      which DeAngelis ruled out of order. He wanted to clarify if more soil would
      help the grass grow.
