  seconds: 2707
  topic: Board Discussion on Immigration Safety Protocols
  desc: The board discussed safety protocols, ICE response training, and public communication
    to reassure vulnerable families.
  children:
  - seconds: 2707
    speaker: Eleni Richardson
    text: Richardson expressed concern over student absences due to fear and advocated
      for accelerating staff training on ICE warrants. She emphasized the need for
      a clear public statement on safety protocols.
  - seconds: 2842
    speaker: Ms. Holman
    text: Holman supported Richardson's suggestions and emphasized the need to let
      families know they are safe and protected. She questioned what language front
      office staff would use in chaotic situations.
  - seconds: 2859
    speaker: Alex Davison
    text: Davison voiced his support for issuing a clear public statement to reassure
      families. He agreed that safety and communication are paramount.
  - seconds: 2868
    speaker: George Risch
    text: Risch asked which committee or subcommittee would be responsible for working
      on this issue. He wanted to know the next steps for the board.
  - seconds: 2881
    speaker: Dr. Entwistle
    text: Dr. Entwistle explained the simplified protocol shared with staff and the
      planned training dates with the university law clinic. He noted that the protocol
      takes the burden off teachers and places it on administrators.
